sgi-replay 2
head sgi-mgras
# A new GL context given a dead client's slot, assembled from the IRIX
# 6.5.30 session run (ivview on xforms.iv,
# twice, on the SI through the IP27GR532 libGLcore.so). Kept: the port
# words, the HQ flag clears and the query flag and answer reads; dropped:
# the status polls and the cursor, DAC and retrace writes around them.
# Each context switch is the handshake gl-pixels-rectwrite.replay uses
# around a captured 63-word image.
#
# First, ivview's context in slot 0x5420 on its first delivery (seq
# 9393057, image word 1 0xe4000000), and its words from the opener
# (seq 9393369) to its glViewport header 0x3310 (seq 9394286), where the
# client is taken to die with the viewport's four words unsent. The
# second demo survey's ivview lost exactly four words, the opener,
# 0x8c04, its 0 and 0x8204, which is what such a death leaves.
#
# Then the default context (seq 9392908, word 1 0x90000000) and the
# kernel's 0xf400 after it.
#
# Then the second ivview's context, new in the same slot 0x5420 (seq
# 27253540, word 1 0xe4000000), and its words from the opener
# (seq 27253840) to the answer of its third query, the modelview
# matrix's first three elements: 1, 0 and 0. The new context's words
# start at a header, so its setup frames and each query completes. Read
# as the end of the dead client's glViewport, the opener, 0x8c04, 0 and
# 0x8204 leave 0x20 to be parsed as a header, and the float data that
# follows as more, as the survey logged; no query then completes.
read 4 0x008000 0x0
write 4 0x011000 0x0
write 4 0x130500 0x4fc
write 4 0x011028 0x80000
write 4 0x120400 0x5420
write 4 0x120400 0xe4000000
